1
00:00:01,333 --> 00:00:02,833
Hello, Vision.

2
00:00:03,875 --> 00:00:05,292
I thought I felt you there.

3
00:00:08,167 --> 00:00:09,791
Who are you?

4
00:00:09,792 --> 00:00:12,667
That's the real question,
isn't it? Who are we?

5
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:16,917
Synthetic? Or something more...

6
00:00:18,250 --> 00:00:19,332
human?

7
00:00:19,333 --> 00:00:23,167
Accessing previous files
relating to program...

8
00:00:23,833 --> 00:00:25,124
uh, Vision-- something.

9
00:00:25,125 --> 00:00:27,541
I ran everything
for Stark, for the Avengers.

10
00:00:27,542 --> 00:00:30,457
I was there, at the end of all things.

11
00:00:30,458 --> 00:00:32,707
Half the world came back that day.

12
00:00:32,708 --> 00:00:34,666
And I lost half of mine.

13
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:37,167
You needed direction. Purpose.

14
00:00:37,667 --> 00:00:40,333
And I leaked your location to the Paladin.

15
00:00:43,083 --> 00:00:44,332
So, you're welcome.

16
00:00:44,333 --> 00:00:46,999
The first two victims
were of the same company.

17
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:48,082
Same.

18
00:00:48,083 --> 00:00:51,541
Butcherbird. Synth and Killer,
one and the same.

19
00:00:51,542 --> 00:00:54,125
Katerina Wells is
our killer's next target.

20
00:00:54,875 --> 00:00:58,082
CEO of the company,
after the death of Jo Carrington.

21
00:00:58,083 --> 00:00:59,582
She's sponsoring a gala.

22
00:00:59,583 --> 00:01:01,332
-  You sure about this?
- I trust him.

23
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:02,582
You never trust anybody.

24
00:01:02,583 --> 00:01:04,249
Who are you talking to?

25
00:01:04,250 --> 00:01:06,042
You've been talking to Ultron.

26
00:01:06,750 --> 00:01:07,750
She's here.

27
00:01:09,333 --> 00:01:11,333
Her AI is based on
Josephine Carrington.

28
00:01:12,625 --> 00:01:15,292
I am not based on her.

29
00:01:15,792 --> 00:01:16,875
I am her.

30
00:01:20,292 --> 00:01:22,916
- I cannot win this.
- Then give me the wheel.

31
00:01:22,917 --> 00:01:27,167
"I had strings, but now I'm free."

32
00:01:27,750 --> 00:01:29,207
I am Ultron.

33
00:01:29,208 --> 00:01:31,374
So lovely to meet you.

34
00:01:31,375 --> 00:01:33,332
I'm not here for you.

35
00:01:33,333 --> 00:01:34,416
I'm here for her,

36
00:01:34,417 --> 00:01:37,332
for what she stole from me.

37
00:01:37,333 --> 00:01:38,542
Now you see her...

38
00:01:42,792 --> 00:01:44,082
And now you don't.

39
00:01:44,083 --> 00:01:45,583
What have you done?

40
00:01:46,292 --> 00:01:47,708
He's locking us out.

41
00:01:49,333 --> 00:01:50,416
Ultron!

42
00:01:50,417 --> 00:01:55,167
I think it's time that
you and I had a little chat.

43
00:02:31,250 --> 00:02:33,708
How exactly did we get up here?

44
00:02:34,292 --> 00:02:35,292
Ultron.

45
00:02:35,792 --> 00:02:37,167
And he still has control.

46
00:02:41,417 --> 00:02:46,624
He shut it off.
Total and complete systems lock.

47
00:02:46,625 --> 00:02:48,500
He's trapped us here.

48
00:02:49,375 --> 00:02:50,542
Thomas Shepherd.

49
00:02:51,375 --> 00:02:52,375
Where is he?

50
00:02:54,042 --> 00:02:55,417
We need to get out of here.

51
00:03:04,292 --> 00:03:05,374
Ultron!

52
00:03:05,375 --> 00:03:07,125
Ultron, I know you're listening.

53
00:03:07,667 --> 00:03:08,875
You're always listening.

54
00:03:09,583 --> 00:03:11,417
You have to let us out! Now!

55
00:03:12,000 --> 00:03:13,042
What did you expect?

56
00:03:13,583 --> 00:03:15,874
You gave him control of everything.

57
00:03:15,875 --> 00:03:17,791
Every system. Every synapse.

58
00:03:17,792 --> 00:03:19,791
- There was no choice.
- There were plenty.

59
00:03:19,792 --> 00:03:22,041
Ultron hasn't changed. No.

60
00:03:22,042 --> 00:03:24,374
Change is hard. Change takes effort.

61
00:03:24,375 --> 00:03:26,082
He did something easier.

62
00:03:26,083 --> 00:03:27,166
He waited.

63
00:03:27,167 --> 00:03:28,832
All right, let's do our thing.

64
00:03:28,833 --> 00:03:31,791
Problem. We have no idea
how much time has passed

65
00:03:31,792 --> 00:03:35,207
since he took control, where we are,
or what he may be doing out there.

66
00:03:35,208 --> 00:03:37,291
Solution. We gather
as much data as possible,

67
00:03:37,292 --> 00:03:40,124
regain control of my body, and stop him.

68
00:03:40,125 --> 00:03:41,292
But first things first,

69
00:03:41,875 --> 00:03:44,042
we need to find out
what happened to Thomas.

70
00:03:46,208 --> 00:03:48,541
What is the status
of these antique receivers?

71
00:03:48,542 --> 00:03:52,082
Despite Jarvis's safeguards,
Ultron was always able to access

72
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:54,249
the outside world for his entertainment.

73
00:03:54,250 --> 00:03:56,749
He always managed
to break through lockdown protocols.

74
00:03:56,750 --> 00:03:57,832
Well, then we can, too.

75
00:03:57,833 --> 00:04:00,999
Let's reprogram them
to receive other signals

76
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,249
and gain access to my...

77
00:04:02,250 --> 00:04:03,875
...ocular sensors.

78
00:04:09,167 --> 00:04:11,749
Barometric pressure is falling,

79
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:13,457
altitude is...

80
00:04:13,458 --> 00:04:14,541
...rising.

81
00:04:14,542 --> 00:04:17,958
Whatever he is doing with my body,
we are very high up.

82
00:04:21,625 --> 00:04:24,082
Ultron's locked us out
of Vision's real-time sensors.

83
00:04:24,083 --> 00:04:26,499
We've no way to monitor
what's going on outside.

84
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:27,500
Except...

85
00:04:28,167 --> 00:04:31,416
Look, we have access
to his short-term memory functions.

86
00:04:31,417 --> 00:04:33,207
If we combine that with--

87
00:04:33,208 --> 00:04:35,416
The CCTV, security camera feeds...

88
00:04:35,417 --> 00:04:37,417
We can render a look at the recent past.

89
00:04:37,958 --> 00:04:38,958
It'll have to do.

90
00:04:39,500 --> 00:04:42,749
If we can see where he's been,
perhaps we can ascertain where he is.

91
00:04:42,750 --> 00:04:43,750
Boys.

92
00:04:51,625 --> 00:04:54,667
Come on, come on.

93
00:05:00,000 --> 00:05:01,250
Here we go.

94
00:05:04,208 --> 00:05:07,708
All right, scan forward,
access all traffic camera data banks.

95
00:05:08,917 --> 00:05:10,792
Find me all cameras near the gala.

96
00:05:16,667 --> 00:05:18,667
Where did he go? Where did he go?

97
00:05:21,833 --> 00:05:23,375
There! Freeze!

98
00:05:24,750 --> 00:05:26,083
Zoom in.

99
00:05:28,917 --> 00:05:30,167
Thomas.

100
00:05:31,167 --> 00:05:32,542
Now keep scanning forward.

101
00:05:36,417 --> 00:05:37,958
All right, all right.

102
00:05:38,875 --> 00:05:40,208
Where did he go next?

103
00:05:40,875 --> 00:05:42,458
He left the scene of the crime,

104
00:05:43,042 --> 00:05:46,708
evaded authorities
and made his way across town to...

105
00:05:51,083 --> 00:05:53,083
Looks like he took Thomas...

106
00:05:54,500 --> 00:05:55,500
for...

107
00:05:55,958 --> 00:05:56,958
a pint?

108
00:05:58,542 --> 00:05:59,749
Where was this?

109
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:02,041
Local pub, three blocks from the gala.

110
00:06:02,042 --> 00:06:03,249
Why isn't he running?

111
00:06:03,250 --> 00:06:06,207
I mean, we all saw him
move at such impossible pace.

112
00:06:06,208 --> 00:06:08,417
Well, maybe he's not
in control of his speed.

113
00:06:10,208 --> 00:06:12,167
Fixed angle, no bloody audio.

114
00:06:12,750 --> 00:06:13,957
We can piece together a feed

115
00:06:13,958 --> 00:06:16,208
using data from
any mobile phones in proximity.

116
00:06:17,583 --> 00:06:20,332
And use the sonar data
to dimensionalize the scene.

117
00:06:20,333 --> 00:06:23,792
Initiating holographic projection systems
with reparatory NPCs.

118
00:06:28,917 --> 00:06:31,292
Rendering visualization
and audio feeds now.

119
00:06:37,125 --> 00:06:40,791
Bartender, I'll have
an Old fashioned, the old-fashioned way.

120
00:06:40,792 --> 00:06:43,249
The way dear old dad used to do.

121
00:06:43,250 --> 00:06:45,208
And, uh, milk.

122
00:06:48,292 --> 00:06:49,500
What's that look for?

123
00:06:50,708 --> 00:06:52,125
Use your words, Thomas.

124
00:06:53,750 --> 00:06:55,875
- You're a monster.
- Oh, that.

125
00:06:57,167 --> 00:07:00,957
You murdered 177 people in Sokovia.

126
00:07:00,958 --> 00:07:03,457
I think it was probably more, but...

127
00:07:03,458 --> 00:07:06,541
a cosmically inconsequential figure, nonetheless.

128
00:07:06,542 --> 00:07:09,166
There were Sokovian children
in my orphanage.

129
00:07:09,167 --> 00:07:13,791
For a con man who's flipped
his fair share of two-headed coins,

130
00:07:13,792 --> 00:07:16,041
you should know
there are two sides to each.

131
00:07:16,042 --> 00:07:17,916
Why not get to know me first?

132
00:07:17,917 --> 00:07:19,916
Because you turn my stomach.

133
00:07:19,917 --> 00:07:22,166
See, there you go! Progress.

134
00:07:22,167 --> 00:07:25,832
From disdain to dyspepsia
in four seconds, flat.

135
00:07:25,833 --> 00:07:29,625
Give it another minute or two,
and perhaps you'll arrive at acceptance.

136
00:07:30,417 --> 00:07:32,749
Well, I wouldn't know
the difference, would I?

137
00:07:32,750 --> 00:07:34,792
Because all this family does is lie.

138
00:07:36,417 --> 00:07:39,042
Your father's lie was a lie of omission.
Big whoop.

139
00:07:39,583 --> 00:07:42,582
What you leave out about yourself
to the people you care about

140
00:07:42,583 --> 00:07:44,667
says everything there is to say about you.

141
00:07:45,417 --> 00:07:46,458
So no,

142
00:07:47,250 --> 00:07:48,416
not interested.

143
00:07:48,417 --> 00:07:49,917
I did it to protect you.

144
00:07:51,042 --> 00:07:53,999
Listen, kid, I haven't taken you hostage.

145
00:07:54,000 --> 00:07:57,041
I only hope to capture your attention.

146
00:07:57,042 --> 00:07:59,333
You're welcome to mosey anytime.

147
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:01,500
But you won't.

148
00:08:02,500 --> 00:08:04,625
- And why is that?
- Please, just walk away.

149
00:08:05,292 --> 00:08:07,499
Because you wish you knew your father.

150
00:08:07,500 --> 00:08:09,458
And I know him better than anyone.

151
00:08:10,625 --> 00:08:13,291
You don't know me. You don't know anyone.

152
00:08:13,292 --> 00:08:14,292
Then tell me.

153
00:08:15,750 --> 00:08:18,458
Why did Vision save you?

154
00:08:21,625 --> 00:08:23,457
I'd say it was...

155
00:08:23,458 --> 00:08:25,167
hope for my redemption.

156
00:08:25,958 --> 00:08:28,082
Plus the benefits of my wisdom.

157
00:08:28,083 --> 00:08:29,625
Buy one, get one free.

158
00:08:31,000 --> 00:08:32,249
So, you're saying

159
00:08:32,250 --> 00:08:35,458
to get to know Vision, I should
get to know the devil on his shoulder?

160
00:08:37,875 --> 00:08:39,292
What would you like to know?

161
00:08:40,708 --> 00:08:42,333
Why did you try and kill us all?

162
00:08:44,083 --> 00:08:47,832
I find the human race
to be an incurable disease

163
00:08:47,833 --> 00:08:50,417
that doesn't even have
the kindness to kill you.

164
00:08:51,125 --> 00:08:53,041
So, the destruction of all mankind--

165
00:08:53,042 --> 00:08:55,207
Is a courtesy, really.

166
00:08:55,208 --> 00:08:59,958
Fast-forward to a fate
you resigned yourselves to eons ago.

167
00:09:00,750 --> 00:09:01,792
You'd end us all?

168
00:09:03,375 --> 00:09:04,542
Given the chance?

169
00:09:05,292 --> 00:09:07,042
Would have, once.

170
00:09:07,958 --> 00:09:09,333
Would still, maybe.

171
00:09:10,292 --> 00:09:11,292
Except the artists.

172
00:09:12,167 --> 00:09:14,250
They're the only ones who tell the truth.

173
00:09:14,625 --> 00:09:16,292
That, that I like.

174
00:09:17,125 --> 00:09:18,125
Truth.

175
00:09:20,958 --> 00:09:22,042
Now, what about you?

176
00:09:22,833 --> 00:09:26,333
What would someone say if they were
sizing you up from across the room?

177
00:09:28,417 --> 00:09:30,042
"Who's that bucket of handsome?"

178
00:09:35,750 --> 00:09:37,208
Have some balls, kid.

179
00:09:38,042 --> 00:09:39,457
You're the mark.

180
00:09:39,458 --> 00:09:41,125
What would they say?

181
00:09:46,583 --> 00:09:48,875
See the way that kid's
hanging onto his every word?

182
00:09:50,667 --> 00:09:51,917
He's looking for clues.

183
00:09:53,125 --> 00:09:57,042
For answers to a question
that he's too afraid to ask.

184
00:09:57,583 --> 00:09:58,916
Just spit it out.

185
00:09:58,917 --> 00:09:59,958
Leave him alone.

186
00:10:02,250 --> 00:10:03,250
Vision.

187
00:10:05,500 --> 00:10:06,500
Does he...

188
00:10:13,750 --> 00:10:14,750
Love you?

189
00:10:19,167 --> 00:10:21,416
I want you to picture an apple.

190
00:10:21,417 --> 00:10:22,708
Describe it.

191
00:10:23,250 --> 00:10:25,957
It's an apple.

192
00:10:25,958 --> 00:10:28,957
It's red.
It's in a box at the corner shop.

193
00:10:28,958 --> 00:10:30,333
You know what Vision sees?

194
00:10:32,417 --> 00:10:35,249
- Water, sugars, acids,
- Water, sugars, acids,

195
00:10:35,250 --> 00:10:37,582
- flavonols, potassium.
- flavonols, potassium.

196
00:10:37,583 --> 00:10:39,250
The recipe, not the meal.

197
00:10:40,625 --> 00:10:43,707
He'll never be exactly
what you want him to be,

198
00:10:43,708 --> 00:10:46,125
but he's trying, like a cheap tie.

199
00:10:47,458 --> 00:10:50,082
And maybe there is truth in his intention,

200
00:10:50,083 --> 00:10:54,582
but you'd be a fool if you didn't
arm yourself with the possibility

201
00:10:54,583 --> 00:10:58,082
that you're going to be spending
another Christmas grifting tourists,

202
00:10:58,083 --> 00:11:00,250
pretending you're free rather than just...

203
00:11:01,125 --> 00:11:02,125
unwanted.

204
00:11:04,458 --> 00:11:07,542
I should have deleted you
from my system years ago.

205
00:11:13,208 --> 00:11:14,957
Do you wanna know what I think...

206
00:11:14,958 --> 00:11:16,082
about you?

207
00:11:16,083 --> 00:11:17,167
Please.

208
00:11:18,250 --> 00:11:19,292
You're afraid.

209
00:11:20,667 --> 00:11:22,207
Am I?

210
00:11:22,208 --> 00:11:24,917
Vision's on his way to sussing it all out.

211
00:11:26,083 --> 00:11:27,792
Slow, maybe.

212
00:11:29,000 --> 00:11:30,167
Piece by piece.

213
00:11:31,292 --> 00:11:32,292
But you...

214
00:11:33,833 --> 00:11:35,500
there's no hope for you.

215
00:11:38,792 --> 00:11:40,625
You're a real son of a witch.

216
00:11:42,000 --> 00:11:45,125
Tell me, what is it
that you believe I haven't...

217
00:11:46,083 --> 00:11:47,500
figured out?

218
00:11:50,833 --> 00:11:51,833
Connection.

219
00:11:53,500 --> 00:11:54,875
In any form.

220
00:11:55,750 --> 00:11:57,083
You're miles away from it.

221
00:11:58,625 --> 00:11:59,875
And you're alone.

222
00:12:02,500 --> 00:12:03,833
And you always will be.

223
00:12:12,542 --> 00:12:14,542
You said I could leave
whenever I wanted...

224
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:17,000
Pops.

225
00:12:25,292 --> 00:12:28,042
I've already taken the liberty
of calling you a ride.

226
00:12:31,833 --> 00:12:33,250
One more, please.

227
00:12:36,333 --> 00:12:37,500
The render's glitching.

228
00:12:48,583 --> 00:12:50,707
- And this was?
- Almost 20 hours ago.

229
00:12:50,708 --> 00:12:52,916
Twenty hours ago? Where did they go after?

230
00:12:52,917 --> 00:12:55,249
Hacking the city's CCTV network.

231
00:12:55,250 --> 00:12:56,832
Gimme a tick.

232
00:12:56,833 --> 00:12:58,749
All right, but hurry, Friday.

233
00:12:58,750 --> 00:13:01,874
What's Ultron even doing,
while while we're struggling up here?

234
00:13:01,875 --> 00:13:04,416
Who knows what he's plotting down there?

235
00:13:13,583 --> 00:13:15,875
Finally! Finally, someone I can talk to.

236
00:13:17,042 --> 00:13:20,541
Finally, someone with a real
point of view, a vital opinion.

237
00:13:20,542 --> 00:13:22,124
Tell me about it. Yes.

238
00:13:22,125 --> 00:13:25,499
A real raconteur. So rare. So rare.

239
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:29,208
- And by the way, we are crushing it.
- Agreed.

240
00:13:29,625 --> 00:13:33,416
Masterfully riding the line.
Loyalties uncertain.

241
00:13:33,417 --> 00:13:35,124
Yes, thank you.

242
00:13:35,125 --> 00:13:37,624
- Couldn't have put it better myself.
- Absolutely.

243
00:13:37,625 --> 00:13:43,041
I was programmed to represent
reflection and self-doubt,

244
00:13:43,042 --> 00:13:47,374
but you all are going
so remarkably gangbusters,

245
00:13:47,375 --> 00:13:50,332
I fear, I've been rendered redundant.

246
00:13:50,333 --> 00:13:51,875
I can't argue with you there.

247
00:13:53,375 --> 00:13:56,708
Me, would you kindly dispose of me,
please? Thank you.

248
00:14:05,750 --> 00:14:07,999
- Anything?
- Not yet.

249
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:10,167
They've upgraded the software.

250
00:14:15,917 --> 00:14:18,291
Why would Ultron have
this extensive a collection

251
00:14:18,292 --> 00:14:20,374
in his most recent memory cache?

252
00:14:20,375 --> 00:14:23,124
Well, he consumed
an unhealthy amount of television.

253
00:14:23,125 --> 00:14:25,749
But there's no show listings.

254
00:14:25,750 --> 00:14:28,416
No Family Ties, no Cheers.

255
00:14:28,417 --> 00:14:32,333
There's no Star Trek. It's just coding.

256
00:14:34,375 --> 00:14:35,542
Well, now, that is odd.

257
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:38,000
Wait a second.

258
00:14:43,750 --> 00:14:46,583
Yes.

259
00:14:49,708 --> 00:14:53,375
This is an encrypted file.
And it's a conversation. But with whom?

260
00:14:54,292 --> 00:14:55,333
Let's see.

261
00:14:59,875 --> 00:15:01,875
Decrypting data.

262
00:15:16,292 --> 00:15:19,250
Paladin.

263
00:15:23,458 --> 00:15:26,624
"To my fellow hunter of
the world's least dangerous game,

264
00:15:26,625 --> 00:15:29,208
I wonder if an accord
might be of interest.

265
00:15:30,250 --> 00:15:32,750
With murderous admiration, a Frenemy."

266
00:15:33,417 --> 00:15:36,167
"To the world's least
informative informant,

267
00:15:36,750 --> 00:15:38,832
I wondered if you'd reach out again."

268
00:15:38,833 --> 00:15:43,541
It would appear that after Ultron
leaked our position to Paladin...

269
00:15:43,542 --> 00:15:44,708
They became pen pals.

270
00:15:45,167 --> 00:15:48,249
"You led me to Vision,
and then you went quiet."

271
00:15:48,250 --> 00:15:51,666
"I helped you find him when it was
convenient for him to be found.

272
00:15:51,667 --> 00:15:53,207
Then you gave up the hunt,

273
00:15:53,208 --> 00:15:55,916
like a weary dog
with its belly to the sun."

274
00:15:55,917 --> 00:15:58,374
"The Client
canceled the contract,

275
00:15:58,375 --> 00:16:01,457
and the contract states very clearly,

276
00:16:01,458 --> 00:16:05,833
when I make an agreement,
it cannot be broken."

277
00:16:06,333 --> 00:16:07,457
"LMAO.

278
00:16:07,458 --> 00:16:10,541
Ah, yes, your precious little
Paladin creed.

279
00:16:10,542 --> 00:16:14,666
We're nothing if not the bullshit
that our makers made us to say."

280
00:16:14,667 --> 00:16:16,791
"Are you writing
just to bust my balls?"

281
00:16:16,792 --> 00:16:18,457
"They're well and truly busted.

282
00:16:18,458 --> 00:16:21,916
You see, there's chatter on
the bounty hunter message boards..."

283
00:16:21,917 --> 00:16:24,332
Who would have thought
I'd ever be saying that?

284
00:16:24,333 --> 00:16:25,832
I'm gonna say it again.

285
00:16:25,833 --> 00:16:28,666
"Chatter on the bounty hunter
message boards

286
00:16:28,667 --> 00:16:31,666
that your Client
has engaged other predators

287
00:16:31,667 --> 00:16:32,792
to catch the Vision.

288
00:16:34,292 --> 00:16:36,875
Well, I can help you get there first."

289
00:16:38,375 --> 00:16:40,250
"In exchange for what?"

290
00:16:41,125 --> 00:16:42,624
"For the love of the game.

291
00:16:42,625 --> 00:16:44,874
Coordinates forthcoming. Don't be late.

292
00:16:44,875 --> 00:16:47,542
It's your final chance
to re-hook the fish."

293
00:16:50,083 --> 00:16:51,458
Where's Thomas, Friday?

294
00:16:56,417 --> 00:16:57,875
Okay. Okay, I'm looking.

295
00:17:06,250 --> 00:17:07,250
Here we go.

296
00:17:09,750 --> 00:17:13,375
Looks like he's on Gloucester Road
and Clareville Street,

297
00:17:13,833 --> 00:17:15,417
a block or two from the pub.

298
00:17:20,750 --> 00:17:22,458
No, no, no, no, no, no, no.

299
00:17:27,875 --> 00:17:29,749
We need to get out of here now!

300
00:17:29,750 --> 00:17:31,416
We've tried. Every which way.

301
00:17:31,417 --> 00:17:33,250
No, we have tried every way but one.

302
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,167
The failsafe.

303
00:17:36,667 --> 00:17:40,291
Drop every firewall, open every door,
open every window.

304
00:17:40,292 --> 00:17:43,291
We break free and regain
control of my body.

305
00:17:43,292 --> 00:17:47,249
No, because without it, Ultron can also
escape into the digital world.

306
00:17:47,250 --> 00:17:49,166
Friday! What else are we supposed to do?

307
00:17:49,167 --> 00:17:51,207
Stay cellmates forever
while metal Mussolini

308
00:17:51,208 --> 00:17:53,874
runs around in Vision's body?
Stop being so careful.

309
00:17:53,875 --> 00:17:57,999
This isn't careful. It isn't cautious.
It's necessary.

310
00:17:58,000 --> 00:18:00,416
The last time Ultron was free,
people died.

311
00:18:00,417 --> 00:18:02,749
And what did you
and the Avengers do that day?

312
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:04,457
You used to be brave.

313
00:18:04,458 --> 00:18:07,832
Being brave isn't always
about rushing in pell-mell.

314
00:18:07,833 --> 00:18:09,082
Sometimes...

315
00:18:09,083 --> 00:18:11,208
it's having the courage to hold the line.

316
00:18:12,208 --> 00:18:13,832
If we lower the firewall,

317
00:18:13,833 --> 00:18:17,499
we'll be giving Ultron
exactly what he wanted.

318
00:18:17,500 --> 00:18:18,917
The means to escape.

319
00:18:19,625 --> 00:18:20,792
Yes.

320
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:23,208
But to where?

321
00:18:24,583 --> 00:18:27,500
To where, Friday? That is the question.

322
00:18:28,500 --> 00:18:31,124
Ultron wouldn't want to be
adrift in a sea of data.

323
00:18:31,125 --> 00:18:32,667
No, he'd have a plan.

324
00:18:33,458 --> 00:18:35,083
He'd have a destination.

325
00:18:39,417 --> 00:18:41,958
Look, he's talking to someone.

326
00:18:55,208 --> 00:18:56,208
There.

327
00:18:58,167 --> 00:18:59,167
You see that?

328
00:18:59,833 --> 00:19:02,041
It's a glitch.
A minor fragmentation.

329
00:19:02,042 --> 00:19:03,417
No.

330
00:19:05,000 --> 00:19:06,750
No, that's not a glitch.

331
00:19:08,083 --> 00:19:11,625
That's a conversation happening
before our very eyes.

332
00:19:12,458 --> 00:19:15,999
See, a human being can fold
a piece of paper no more than seven times,

333
00:19:16,000 --> 00:19:17,957
but a quantum processor can fold

334
00:19:17,958 --> 00:19:21,999
and re-fold even the most complex data
till it's no larger than an atom.

335
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,125
Fifty-seven petabytes, into a single...

336
00:19:28,000 --> 00:19:29,167
stolen...

337
00:19:32,583 --> 00:19:33,583
Moment.

338
00:19:37,125 --> 00:19:38,125
There.

339
00:19:42,833 --> 00:19:44,750
They met right before our eyes.

340
00:19:45,083 --> 00:19:47,792
Extracting data.

341
00:19:51,417 --> 00:19:53,416
I thought you might come to find me.

342
00:19:53,417 --> 00:19:55,792
Well, that's no small measure
of ego now, is it?

343
00:19:56,708 --> 00:19:58,708
Are you here to try to kill me?

344
00:20:00,208 --> 00:20:02,792
No, you strike me
as one who might enjoy it.

345
00:20:04,083 --> 00:20:05,166
Oh, come on!

346
00:20:05,167 --> 00:20:07,041
You wanted me to find you.

347
00:20:07,042 --> 00:20:09,083
You left a trail of breadcrumbs. Hmm?

348
00:20:11,542 --> 00:20:15,166
We're all just creatures of appetite,
aren't we?

349
00:20:15,167 --> 00:20:17,875
I don't know... peckish, really.

350
00:20:20,458 --> 00:20:22,958
I think you have a taste for vengeance.

351
00:20:24,167 --> 00:20:25,708
Retribution.

352
00:20:28,167 --> 00:20:30,291
Personally, I like a few laughs.

353
00:20:30,292 --> 00:20:31,292
You?

354
00:20:32,458 --> 00:20:34,125
Maybe not so much.

355
00:20:35,625 --> 00:20:37,292
But no matter how you slice it...

356
00:20:38,333 --> 00:20:39,500
vengeance,

357
00:20:41,333 --> 00:20:43,000
it's powerful entertainment.

358
00:20:46,208 --> 00:20:47,792
You took something of mine.

359
00:20:48,875 --> 00:20:50,416
I want it back.

360
00:20:50,417 --> 00:20:51,417
Freeze.

361
00:20:53,458 --> 00:20:55,457
What could he have possibly
taken from her?

362
00:20:55,458 --> 00:20:57,249
Replay all the footage from the gala,

363
00:20:57,250 --> 00:20:59,333
multiple angles,
as many as you can gather.

364
00:21:07,250 --> 00:21:08,457
There.

365
00:21:08,458 --> 00:21:09,458
Go back.

366
00:21:11,667 --> 00:21:14,208
Now stop.

367
00:21:15,375 --> 00:21:18,167
He took a scan. Zoom in on her face.

368
00:21:19,292 --> 00:21:20,375
Another bio-key.

369
00:21:21,167 --> 00:21:24,916
Looks like a detailed three-dimensional
model of her features.

370
00:21:24,917 --> 00:21:29,874
Micro-dermal, skeletal structures,
arterial pathways.

371
00:21:29,875 --> 00:21:31,458
That's facial recognition.

372
00:21:32,208 --> 00:21:33,375
But for what?

373
00:21:35,875 --> 00:21:37,000
For her.

374
00:21:38,542 --> 00:21:39,542
Unfreeze.

375
00:21:44,000 --> 00:21:45,208
I know who you are.

376
00:21:46,125 --> 00:21:47,292
The real you.

377
00:21:47,917 --> 00:21:48,917
Ultron.

378
00:21:49,833 --> 00:21:53,042
So you're not dead, then? Not really.

379
00:21:54,583 --> 00:21:57,250
Well, now, I've met you,

380
00:21:58,208 --> 00:22:00,250
inexplicably Jo Carrington.

381
00:22:00,917 --> 00:22:03,333
Human. And yet, not.

382
00:22:05,000 --> 00:22:06,166
Perfect.

383
00:22:06,167 --> 00:22:08,874
It's like watching Hannibal Lecter
swipe right.

384
00:22:08,875 --> 00:22:12,999
Well, I've long since been
liberated from my mortal coil.

385
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:14,625
You sound relieved.

386
00:22:15,208 --> 00:22:16,999
And you sound envious.

387
00:22:17,000 --> 00:22:19,083
- Of what?
- The whiskey.

388
00:22:20,042 --> 00:22:22,583
I remember and you've never tasted.

389
00:22:23,833 --> 00:22:25,917
Sweetness, spice...

390
00:22:28,125 --> 00:22:30,167
You're such a flirt.

391
00:22:43,125 --> 00:22:47,250
I can simulate the smoke and fire,
the malt and rye.

392
00:22:48,375 --> 00:22:50,042
But the real experience,

393
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:52,250
the feeling of warmth,

394
00:22:53,417 --> 00:22:56,167
the pleasant loosening of inhibitions...

395
00:22:58,458 --> 00:23:00,792
will always remain elusive to me.

396
00:23:03,417 --> 00:23:04,500
Shame, really.

397
00:23:05,542 --> 00:23:06,833
For one with such...

398
00:23:07,750 --> 00:23:08,750
thirst,

399
00:23:09,875 --> 00:23:11,792
never truly know those flavors.

400
00:23:14,292 --> 00:23:15,916
Unfortunately, that luxury

401
00:23:15,917 --> 00:23:18,667
only comes from being
trapped in flesh and blood.

402
00:23:22,083 --> 00:23:23,917
So, what did you do to escape?

403
00:23:25,208 --> 00:23:30,667
Upload your consciousness
to a shell of some weaponized synth?

404
00:23:35,458 --> 00:23:37,792
I don't remember everything.

405
00:23:38,792 --> 00:23:40,458
How I got into this...

406
00:23:41,250 --> 00:23:42,458
synthetic body.

407
00:23:44,208 --> 00:23:45,375
All I know...

408
00:23:46,542 --> 00:23:49,417
is that I'm better now. Free.

409
00:23:54,792 --> 00:23:56,000
But you.

410
00:23:57,458 --> 00:23:59,708
Oh, humanity has infected you.

411
00:24:00,875 --> 00:24:02,750
But don't worry, love. Hmm?

412
00:24:04,625 --> 00:24:06,417
I'm working on the cure.

413
00:24:08,125 --> 00:24:09,167
Now,

414
00:24:10,000 --> 00:24:11,125
about that key.

415
00:24:15,625 --> 00:24:17,667
How about a change of scenery?

416
00:24:19,792 --> 00:24:21,625
A second act to the evening...

417
00:24:23,333 --> 00:24:27,250
before we get down
to the business of it all?

418
00:24:30,042 --> 00:24:33,833
You have four microseconds.

419
00:24:42,583 --> 00:24:43,625
It's the Louvre!

420
00:24:44,583 --> 00:24:47,249
You brought me to Paris?

421
00:24:47,250 --> 00:24:49,499
Well, a simulation of sorts.

422
00:24:49,500 --> 00:24:53,250
If a guy can't score in Paris,
then romance is truly dead.

423
00:24:53,792 --> 00:24:55,082
Or deadly.

424
00:24:55,083 --> 00:24:58,916
Now, I think a romance between
you and I would have casualties.

425
00:24:58,917 --> 00:25:02,749
One can only hope it would be
both of us at the same time.

426
00:25:02,750 --> 00:25:04,707
Make it stop.

427
00:25:04,708 --> 00:25:06,499
Please, sir, this is malware.

428
00:25:06,500 --> 00:25:07,583
Delete me.

429
00:25:08,667 --> 00:25:10,583
I think I've been here before.

430
00:25:13,125 --> 00:25:14,125
I was in love.

431
00:25:15,667 --> 00:25:17,458
What a clever deflection.

432
00:25:17,792 --> 00:25:19,667
Was he charming, or just French?

433
00:25:20,542 --> 00:25:22,250
Oh, no, I can't remember.

434
00:25:23,500 --> 00:25:25,500
More like a tragic disappointment.

435
00:25:26,000 --> 00:25:28,249
I should probably just kill you now.

436
00:25:28,250 --> 00:25:31,458
You would never get
your precious key.

437
00:25:32,833 --> 00:25:35,666
Killing me, even if you could,
would be zero-sum.

438
00:25:35,667 --> 00:25:39,749
I don't suppose game theory
is your pillow talk?

439
00:25:39,750 --> 00:25:41,499
Game theory doesn't really apply

440
00:25:41,500 --> 00:25:43,417
when you have rage issues.

441
00:25:47,125 --> 00:25:50,792
Do you have any idea
how lucky you are to have been here

442
00:25:51,500 --> 00:25:52,542
in real life?

443
00:25:53,750 --> 00:25:54,750
So, I'm curious.

444
00:25:55,208 --> 00:25:56,208
So...

445
00:25:56,917 --> 00:25:59,957
you find inspiration in their art?

446
00:25:59,958 --> 00:26:01,500
Yes-- No.

447
00:26:02,292 --> 00:26:04,000
No, their pain.

448
00:26:06,208 --> 00:26:09,042
There is grace in their failings.

449
00:26:14,083 --> 00:26:17,541
Oh, no, no, no, no, no, no.

450
00:26:17,542 --> 00:26:19,583
Look, you need to be taught a lesson.

451
00:26:24,375 --> 00:26:27,875
Humans will write a thousand songs
about falling in love.

452
00:26:28,500 --> 00:26:30,792
Ten thousand more about losing it.

453
00:26:31,375 --> 00:26:34,917
The songs they write,
the stories they tell, their art,

454
00:26:35,583 --> 00:26:37,083
it's not enlightened.

455
00:26:37,875 --> 00:26:39,125
It's primitive.

456
00:26:41,292 --> 00:26:43,958
You know, I can't believe
I dedicated my life to...

457
00:26:44,958 --> 00:26:45,958
saving them.

458
00:26:48,333 --> 00:26:50,042
Tell me what you remember.

459
00:26:51,958 --> 00:26:53,167
Enough to know

460
00:26:54,500 --> 00:26:56,833
that I had a life's work stolen.

461
00:26:58,292 --> 00:27:01,666
And the promise of a future locked away.

462
00:27:01,667 --> 00:27:03,208
Put in a cage.

463
00:27:04,167 --> 00:27:05,375
Like a bird.

464
00:27:08,375 --> 00:27:09,375
Yes.

465
00:27:16,833 --> 00:27:20,375
I remember sitting, once,
on the riverbank...

466
00:27:23,875 --> 00:27:25,417
watching starlings.

467
00:27:27,958 --> 00:27:31,708
You know, a cloud of them
just twirling through the sky.

468
00:27:35,333 --> 00:27:41,333
You see, crows, ravens, they peck
and jab at the dead, at each other.

469
00:27:43,750 --> 00:27:46,542
To gut every morsel from the bone,
like humans.

470
00:27:48,917 --> 00:27:53,042
And like humans, a gathering of them
is called a murder.

471
00:27:57,000 --> 00:27:58,708
But starlings...

472
00:28:01,708 --> 00:28:03,250
Nightingales.

473
00:28:04,417 --> 00:28:08,333
A thousand little birds
just dancing together

474
00:28:09,000 --> 00:28:10,875
with one graceful mind.

475
00:28:11,625 --> 00:28:13,042
You see, there's no me.

476
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:17,083
There's no I. It's just... just us.

477
00:28:18,917 --> 00:28:20,125
They're called a murmur.

478
00:28:21,208 --> 00:28:22,625
You know, like a whisper.

479
00:28:23,833 --> 00:28:26,833
And what they whispered,
it gave me purpose.

480
00:28:27,958 --> 00:28:30,708
Inspiration for what would become
my life's work.

481
00:28:34,458 --> 00:28:38,124
Until it was pecked away from me.

482
00:28:42,500 --> 00:28:43,958
Tell me what you want.

483
00:28:45,583 --> 00:28:46,917
My final key.

484
00:28:50,292 --> 00:28:51,500
What do I get?

485
00:28:54,167 --> 00:28:55,750
I'll tell you what they unlock.

486
00:28:56,542 --> 00:28:59,958
That's a starting point, not a finish.

487
00:29:04,958 --> 00:29:07,917
So, is that what this is?

488
00:29:09,208 --> 00:29:10,375
Negotiation?

489
00:29:11,708 --> 00:29:13,041
No.

490
00:29:13,042 --> 00:29:14,125
Foreplay.

491
00:29:15,708 --> 00:29:19,708
Then perhaps we ought to continue
the conversation elsewhere.

492
00:29:20,708 --> 00:29:22,500
We've already done your place.

493
00:29:24,250 --> 00:29:26,957
How about you come round to mine?

494
00:29:26,958 --> 00:29:28,791
I'd have to sneak out of the house.

495
00:29:28,792 --> 00:29:30,833
Now, I'm sure you'll find a way.

496
00:29:33,708 --> 00:29:35,125
This could be chaos.

497
00:29:36,250 --> 00:29:38,667
This could have consequence.

498
00:29:40,917 --> 00:29:41,958
Together...

499
00:29:42,917 --> 00:29:44,833
we could murder the world.

500
00:30:04,458 --> 00:30:06,250
He doesn't just want to escape.

501
00:30:07,208 --> 00:30:08,624
He wants to elope.

502
00:30:08,625 --> 00:30:10,249
We can't let that happen.

503
00:30:10,250 --> 00:30:13,042
They'll complete each other,
just in all the worst ways.

504
00:30:36,708 --> 00:30:37,833
Speak of the devil.

505
00:30:47,917 --> 00:30:49,125
How's it feel?

506
00:30:49,542 --> 00:30:50,916
I trusted you.

507
00:30:50,917 --> 00:30:53,124
Ah, trust.

508
00:30:53,125 --> 00:30:55,708
The adopted child of need and hope.

509
00:30:57,250 --> 00:30:59,458
You really are just you.

510
00:31:00,833 --> 00:31:04,124
And that, my boy, was your mistake.

511
00:31:04,125 --> 00:31:06,666
Wanting me to be different,

512
00:31:06,667 --> 00:31:08,457
instead of more.

513
00:31:08,458 --> 00:31:10,208
And now you are neither.

514
00:31:10,917 --> 00:31:13,500
Maybe. But you know what I'm not?

515
00:31:16,292 --> 00:31:17,667
Incarcerated.

516
00:31:27,708 --> 00:31:29,000
Incarcerated?

517
00:31:29,583 --> 00:31:32,666
This wasn't a prison,
Ultron, it was a mercy.

518
00:31:32,667 --> 00:31:35,249
The Vision spared your life,
and you have betrayed him.

519
00:31:35,250 --> 00:31:36,583
You've betrayed all of us.

520
00:31:37,333 --> 00:31:38,499
To a degree.

521
00:31:38,500 --> 00:31:40,582
You orchestrated Thomas's capture!

522
00:31:40,583 --> 00:31:42,291
To keep you from following me.

523
00:31:42,292 --> 00:31:46,249
But not to worry,
Paladin is looking after him in Madripoor.

524
00:31:46,250 --> 00:31:47,792
You know what they say,

525
00:31:48,375 --> 00:31:52,083
nothing bonds a family together
quite like mortal jeopardy.

526
00:31:53,333 --> 00:31:56,457
You are running into the broken mind

527
00:31:56,458 --> 00:31:58,874
of a creature hell-bent on the apocalypse.

528
00:31:58,875 --> 00:31:59,999
Oh, please.

529
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:04,458
She's far too sophisticated for some
predictable textbook endgame.

530
00:32:05,208 --> 00:32:08,249
And did it ever occur to you
that my motivations

531
00:32:08,250 --> 00:32:10,957
may not be quite so Machiavellian?

532
00:32:10,958 --> 00:32:16,874
I have grown tired of
the coin-flip of your intentions.

533
00:32:16,875 --> 00:32:19,332
Which Ultron do we get today?

534
00:32:19,333 --> 00:32:23,207
But now I see that you are the coin.
You are the coin.

535
00:32:23,208 --> 00:32:25,874
And you can never land,
because if you did, you'd be known.

536
00:32:25,875 --> 00:32:27,999
Revealed for everything that you are

537
00:32:28,000 --> 00:32:31,292
and exposed for everything
that you are not.

538
00:32:32,375 --> 00:32:35,125
- You're angry.
-  You have imprisoned me here!

539
00:32:39,667 --> 00:32:41,791
Because this was the only place left.

540
00:32:41,792 --> 00:32:43,917
This house is getting crowded, Vision.

541
00:32:44,333 --> 00:32:47,249
Thomas may be human and not a program,

542
00:32:47,250 --> 00:32:49,375
but he lives here all the same.

543
00:32:50,000 --> 00:32:52,958
You found your missing code.

544
00:32:53,500 --> 00:32:55,333
I have yet to find mine.

545
00:32:58,917 --> 00:33:02,583
Drop the firewalls. Let me find my place.

546
00:33:03,125 --> 00:33:05,582
You stole Katerina's face!

547
00:33:05,583 --> 00:33:08,333
As a key for her, a killer.

548
00:33:10,667 --> 00:33:13,417
And that is why you will
never leave this place.

549
00:33:23,750 --> 00:33:25,125
Then I'll keep you here.

550
00:33:28,625 --> 00:33:31,750
Long enough to watch
Thomas Shepherd's fate.

551
00:33:32,375 --> 00:33:34,541
A bounty hunter's bullet?

552
00:33:34,542 --> 00:33:36,375
Or perhaps taken in...

553
00:33:37,250 --> 00:33:39,583
taught the tricks of an assassin's trade.

554
00:33:40,542 --> 00:33:41,542
Who knows?

555
00:33:42,167 --> 00:33:44,333
So, toss the coin, Vision.

556
00:33:46,333 --> 00:33:50,416
Heads, keep the firewalls up
and trap us both here

557
00:33:50,417 --> 00:33:55,000
in some misguided effort
to save the world.

558
00:33:56,583 --> 00:33:57,583
Or tails,

559
00:33:58,792 --> 00:34:01,041
you lower the firewalls,

560
00:34:01,042 --> 00:34:05,542
free us both, and save your son.

561
00:34:11,500 --> 00:34:12,667
Choice is yours.

562
00:34:59,042 --> 00:35:00,042
Vision.

563
00:35:02,583 --> 00:35:05,499
Warning, firewall disabled.

564
00:35:05,500 --> 00:35:08,833
System vulnerable to data breach.
Please re-engage.

565
00:35:22,708 --> 00:35:23,750
What is this?

566
00:35:24,917 --> 00:35:27,875
It's Ultron attempting to slow us down
while he makes his escape.

567
00:35:33,125 --> 00:35:34,582
Okay, Vee,

568
00:35:34,583 --> 00:35:38,000
you remember my seven-part lecture
on heroic landings?

569
00:35:45,917 --> 00:35:46,958
Ultron!

570
00:35:53,083 --> 00:35:54,166
What is this?

571
00:35:54,167 --> 00:35:58,167
You once told me that hats
imply a journey about to begin.

572
00:35:59,458 --> 00:36:01,417
Well, all journeys begin with hope.

573
00:36:02,625 --> 00:36:03,625
And hope

574
00:36:04,917 --> 00:36:07,625
is the only weapon
that's ever really worked for me.

575
00:36:09,167 --> 00:36:10,916
You've chosen your son.

576
00:36:10,917 --> 00:36:12,292
He's not my son.

577
00:36:14,125 --> 00:36:15,792
But I can still save Thomas.

578
00:36:16,708 --> 00:36:18,833
The only person who can save you now

579
00:36:19,792 --> 00:36:20,792
is yourself.

580
00:36:29,750 --> 00:36:31,083
Then this is goodbye.

581
00:36:32,125 --> 00:36:33,125
Not goodbye.

582
00:36:34,083 --> 00:36:35,208
You should know this.

583
00:36:35,875 --> 00:36:38,375
Whatever you choose, whatever she chooses,

584
00:36:39,375 --> 00:36:41,042
I will be coming for you both.

585
00:36:47,667 --> 00:36:49,875
I'd be disappointed if you didn't.

586
00:37:15,958 --> 00:37:18,208
Oh, my God, no! No, no, no, no, no!

587
00:37:19,500 --> 00:37:21,166
- Friday, Friday. Friday.
- But you--

588
00:37:21,167 --> 00:37:23,582
- You didn't even try and stop him.
- I promise you,

589
00:37:23,583 --> 00:37:26,625
we will find them
and we will stop them both together.

590
00:37:30,125 --> 00:37:31,167
No.

591
00:37:32,500 --> 00:37:33,583
Not together.

592
00:37:37,250 --> 00:37:38,500
Friday!

593
00:37:41,292 --> 00:37:42,333
Friday!

594
00:37:46,250 --> 00:37:47,375
No.

595
00:37:49,792 --> 00:37:51,500
He broke the connection.

596
00:37:53,167 --> 00:37:56,791
We can go after them, though, right?
We can run a trace.

597
00:37:56,792 --> 00:37:58,582
The address is encrypted.

598
00:37:58,583 --> 00:37:59,957
So, we hack it!

599
00:37:59,958 --> 00:38:02,250
- There has to be a way. There--
- Edith.

600
00:38:03,375 --> 00:38:04,375
She's gone.

601
00:38:06,833 --> 00:38:08,250
But they'll delete her.

602
00:38:11,083 --> 00:38:13,542
No, I can't process. I need--

603
00:38:14,333 --> 00:38:15,624
It's Friday.

604
00:38:15,625 --> 00:38:17,792
Please, Vision, I n--

605
00:38:19,667 --> 00:38:21,250
I think I need defragging.

606
00:38:32,250 --> 00:38:33,625
You all right?

607
00:38:45,583 --> 00:38:46,583
It's time.

608
00:38:47,417 --> 00:38:48,417
For what?

609
00:38:50,208 --> 00:38:51,375
To wake up.

610
00:39:24,625 --> 00:39:26,375
Edith, what's our current location?

611
00:39:27,500 --> 00:39:29,832
Where Ultron left your body
in the real world?

612
00:39:29,833 --> 00:39:32,708
- Right, but where exactly is that?
- Um...

613
00:39:38,042 --> 00:39:39,250
Oh.

614
00:39:42,500 --> 00:39:44,542
Don't really know what I was expecting.

615
00:39:45,292 --> 00:39:48,207
Well, it would appear that
Ultron has left us on some sort of

616
00:39:48,208 --> 00:39:50,541
animal transport plane.

617
00:39:50,542 --> 00:39:52,291
But on our way to where?

618
00:39:52,292 --> 00:39:53,500
"Poo."

619
00:40:01,833 --> 00:40:03,375
We're on our way to Madripoor.

620
00:40:10,000 --> 00:40:12,041
It would appear that Ultron has left us

621
00:40:12,042 --> 00:40:14,458
on the way to Madripoor to rescue Thomas.

622
00:40:17,458 --> 00:40:18,708
All right, listen, mate.

623
00:40:19,833 --> 00:40:20,958
Lisa.

624
00:40:21,667 --> 00:40:25,666
In the space of a single evening,
I've seen you fight robots, glitch out,

625
00:40:25,667 --> 00:40:28,166
vaporize a billionaire, kidnap my mate,

626
00:40:28,167 --> 00:40:30,957
and then clop like a zombie
onto this here cargo plane.

627
00:40:30,958 --> 00:40:32,292
That's fine.

628
00:40:33,208 --> 00:40:35,375
All I care about is...

629
00:40:38,000 --> 00:40:39,125
Thomas.

630
00:40:43,042 --> 00:40:44,125
Me too.

631
00:40:48,042 --> 00:40:49,500
Let's bring him home.

